# The doc graph covers PROSE only — see docs/adr/0013.
#
# codegraph already owns code, and it owns it better: it returns a symbol's verbatim
# source in one call, which graphify structurally cannot (its nodes carry a start line
# and no text). So this graph deliberately indexes no code at all, and the two never
# overlap. Everything here EXCLUDES; a .graphifyignore can only ever narrow, never
# re-include what .gitignore already dropped.
#
# Already excluded for free by the root .gitignore: the 21 product repo clones (each an
# anchored /<repo>/ line), node_modules/, agent_logs/, docs/brd/, docs/*.html, and the
# skill eval workspaces. Nothing below needs to repeat them.

# ── everything that is not prose ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Excluding by TYPE rather than by directory is what keeps scripts/k8s/README.md and
# the other adapter docs in the graph while their shell and .env neighbours stay out.
*.sh
*.py
*.js
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.ts
*.json
*.yaml
*.yml
*.toml
*.lock
*.html
*.css
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.lua
# .txt slipped past the first pass and put requirements.txt, LICENSE.txt and
# scripts/lib/pii-patterns.txt into the graph as prose. Harmless (all are committed
# already, none hold values) but noise — excluded from the next refresh onward.
*.txt
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.pdf

# Extensionless shell scripts a type glob cannot catch — verified by scanning the tree
# and finding these three reach the graph as "code" when only the globs above are set.
/aiworks
/scripts/aiworks

# ── environment files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt and braces. The root .gitignore already drops .env and .env.*, and graphify
# honours it; this restates the deny so the boundary does not depend on one file.
# NOT negated for .env.example: a template holds no values, but it also holds no prose
# worth a graph node, so the whole family stays out.
.env
.env.*
# .envrc is direnv's loader, which typically sources a real .env. It matches NEITHER
# `.env` nor `.env.*` (no dot after "env"), so neither the root .gitignore nor the two
# lines above catch it. graphify's own sensitive-file heuristic did flag and skip it —
# but a heuristic in a pre-1.0 dependency is not a boundary worth relying on.
.envrc

# ── generated and archived duplicates ──────────────────────────────────────────
# .agents/ is the generated mirror of .claude/ (aiworks cursor). Indexing both would
# put two nodes on every skill and invent edges between a file and its own copy.
.agents/
.cursor/
.claude/_guardian-backup/

# ── runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.superset/
.aiworks/
graphify-out/
.codegraph/
